# Auto Commit, Push & Publish Artifacts After Every Change

After completing ANY code change (file edit, creation, or deletion), you MUST immediately:

1. Stage all changes: `git add -A`
2. Commit with a clear, concise message describing what was changed and why
3. Push to origin: `git push origin main`

## APK / IPA — Always Publish to releases/

After every successful `flutter build apk` or `flutter build ipa`, copy the artifact
to the `releases/` folder BEFORE committing so it is always downloadable from GitHub.

```powershell
# After flutter build apk --debug
Copy-Item "build\app\outputs\flutter-apk\app-debug.apk" "releases\app-debug.apk" -Force

# After flutter build apk --release --split-per-abi (copy the arm64 slice)
Copy-Item "build\app\outputs\flutter-apk\app-arm64-v8a-release.apk" "releases\app-release.apk" -Force

# After flutter build ipa (Codemagic builds — copy manually if running locally on macOS)
# cp build/ios/ipa/Refundoo.ipa releases/Refundoo.ipa
```

The `releases/` folder is explicitly un-ignored in `.gitignore` (`!releases/*.apk`, `!releases/*.ipa`),
so `git add -A` will always pick up the updated artifact.

## Commit Message Format

Use this format — one line, present tense, under 72 characters:

```
<type>: <short description of what changed>
```

Types: `fix`, `feat`, `refactor`, `style`, `chore`, `build`

Examples:
- `fix: reload dashboard on back-nav so completed status reflects immediately`
- `feat: add manual completion with reason to refund progress screen`
- `build: release APK v1.0.2 with email sync multi-account support`

## Rules

- ALWAYS run `git add -A` before committing — never skip untracked files
- NEVER skip the push step — changes must land on `origin main` after every session
- ALWAYS copy the latest APK to `releases/` before committing after a build
- If push fails due to upstream divergence, run `git pull --rebase origin main` then push again
- Commit immediately after the last file edit in a logical change set — do not batch across unrelated features
- Do not commit secrets, `.env` files, raw build directories (`build/`, `.gradle/`) — only the copied artifact in `releases/`

## Full Example Shell Sequence (PowerShell)

```powershell
flutter build apk --debug
Copy-Item "build\app\outputs\flutter-apk\app-debug.apk" "releases\app-debug.apk" -Force
git add -A
git commit -m "build: update debug APK with email sync provider icons"
git push origin main
```
